### Case: valid-call-transformed / response-really-converted
###
### The SOAP envelope, written as JSON. The gateway converts this body to XML
### (adding the namespace declarations from root_attributes), calls the handler on
### <SOAP_HANDLER_PATH>, and converts the XML response back to JSON.
###
### Replace m:Operation and m:param with the operation and ELEMENT NAMES the SOAP
### handler reads. If
### they don't, you typically get a 200 with an empty result rather than an error —
### which reads as "no data" and is actually "wrong request".
###
### accept: application/json is REQUIRED — the response transform is
### content-negotiated and does nothing without it.
###
### Expect 200, content-type application/json, AND a body with no angle brackets.
POST {{GATEWAY}}/locations
content-type: application/json
accept: application/json

{"soap:Envelope":{"soap:Body":{"m:Operation":{"m:param":"value"}}}}

### curl equivalent:
###   curl -i -X POST {{GATEWAY}}/locations \
###     -H 'content-type: application/json' -H 'accept: application/json' \
###     -d '{"soap:Envelope":{"soap:Body":{"m:Operation":{"m:param":"value"}}}}'
